                <mxCell id="user-stories-title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=27;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#18181b;align=left;" value="USER STORIES - minimal effort GitHub connection" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="70" width="1500" x="1400" y="3580" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="user-story-1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=5;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;fontColor=#18181b;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" value="US01 - Connect GitHub&#10;&#10;As a user, I want to choose Add connection and sign in with GitHub, so I can connect my account without registering an App or entering App IDs, client secrets, callbacks or tokens.&#10;&#10;Laomedo does the work: Laomedo opens GitHub, handles the return, verifies the account and saves the connection after the required approvals." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="260" width="1500" x="1400" y="4740" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="user-story-2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=5;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;fontColor=#18181b;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" value="US02 - Choose repository access&#10;&#10;As a user, I want to choose which repositories Laomedo may read, so I stay in control of access.&#10;&#10;Laomedo does the work: Laomedo discovers available repositories and presents clear choices. I make the required access decisions; I do not copy repository IDs or repeat equivalent choices unnecessarily." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="260" width="1500" x="1400" y="5680" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="user-story-3" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=5;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;fontColor=#18181b;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" value="US03 - Use a saved connection&#10;&#10;As a user, I want to select a saved GitHub connection and use its permitted repositories, so I do not have to sign in or configure it again each time.&#10;&#10;Laomedo does the work: Laomedo remembers the account and consent, checks current access, and renews credentials automatically when supported." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="260" width="1500" x="1400" y="3800" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="user-story-4" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=5;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;fontColor=#18181b;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" value="US04 - Add another account&#10;&#10;As a user, I want to add another GitHub account through the same Add connection flow, so I can use multiple accounts without disturbing existing connections.&#10;&#10;Laomedo does the work: Laomedo manages each connection separately and shows which account and repositories belong to it. Duplicate-account handling remains an open decision." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="260" width="1500" x="1400" y="4090" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="user-story-5" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=5;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;fontColor=#18181b;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" value="US05 - Recover access&#10;&#10;As a user, I want a clear explanation and the appropriate recovery action when access fails, so I can continue with minimal effort.&#10;&#10;Laomedo does the work: Laomedo preserves my selections and performs safe automatic recovery where possible. An offline check does not force a new login. It asks me to authorize again only when needed, for the correct saved account." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="260" width="1500" x="1400" y="8500" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="user-story-6" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=5;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;fontColor=#18181b;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" value="US06 - Disconnect an account&#10;&#10;As a user, I want to disconnect a selected GitHub connection, so Laomedo stops using its access.&#10;&#10;Laomedo does the work: Laomedo blocks further private reads, clears private views and removes its stored credentials. It reports incomplete cleanup honestly and does not claim to revoke GitHub consent." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="260" width="1500" x="1400" y="6620" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="user-stories-responsibility" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=5;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;fontColor=#18181b;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;fillColor=#eff6ff;strokeColor=#93c5fd;" value="SHARED RULE&#10;&#10;The user only makes identity, authorization and repository-access decisions that cannot appropriately be automated. Laomedo handles integration provisioning, navigation, verification, secure credential storage, renewal and connection state.&#10;&#10;Normal GitHub sign-in must not require the user to register an App or supply App credentials. A personal access token is an optional advanced alternative under Add connection, not a prerequisite.&#10;&#10;These stories record the owner's intended experience. Secure provisioning architecture remains to be resolved; this is not a claim that it is implemented. Existing graph/screens are unchanged and may need later alignment." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="390" width="1500" x="1400" y="7560" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="screen-gallery-title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#18181b;fontSize=16;spacing=0;fontSize=30;fontColor=#18181b;fontStyle=1;align=left;" value="SCREEN GALLERY - one state per viewport" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="45" width="1200" x="50" y="3580" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="screen-gallery-note" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#18181b;fontSize=16;spacing=0;fontSize=17;fontColor=#52525b;fontStyle=0;align=left;" value="White backgrounds, 8 px spacing rhythm, 44 px actions. Identifiers match the graph; annotations stay outside the product UI." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="34" width="1200" x="50" y="3635" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
